## How to read these mocks

Each mock is the content and layout, not the final pixels. Numbers are made up but consistent with each other. Requirement ids point at [token-metering-requirement.smd](../requirements/token-metering-requirement.smd), and the data behind each screen is in [token-metering-design.smd](token-metering-design.smd).

The hover card follows the VS Code status bar hover, as the Copilot status card does. A status bar hover can show Markdown, theme icons, links to commands and coloured text, but no buttons, inputs or charts. Its renderer does allow `data:` images, so each bar is a thin SVG (4 px high, fixed colours since an image cannot read theme variables), and actions are links. The ASCII mocks below show the bars as blocks. The panel is a webview and has none of those limits.

## Status bar item

| State                                 | Text                                  | Click                 |
| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | --------------------- |
| `.smd` file active, metering off      | `$(hubot) 6.3k → 2.1k tok`            | Opens the agent view  |
| Metering on, reads in the last 7 days | `$(hubot) 6.3k → 2.1k tok · 14 reads` | Opens the meter panel |
| Metering on, no reads yet             | `$(hubot) 6.3k → 2.1k tok · 0 reads`  | Opens the meter panel |
| Any other file                        | Hidden                                | —                     |

The arrow reads as "without smd → with smd". The part before the arrow is the raw file and the part after it is the agent view, both estimates for the active file (R12).

## Hover card

### Metering off

This is the phase 1 card, already prototyped on `feat/token-meter`.

```text
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 🤖 Agent token meter                                 │
│                                                      │
│ 67% fewer tokens with smd                            │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ Without smd · raw file          ≈6,312 tok           │
│ ████████████████████████                    (red)    │
│ With smd · agent view           ≈2,104 tok · 67% fewer│
│ ████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░                    (blue)   │
│ With smd · brief view           ≈1,204 tok · 81% fewer│
│ █████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░                    (green)  │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ 👁 Agent view · ⚡ Brief · ☰ Left out · ⧉ Copy        │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ Measure real agent reads?  ▸ Turn on metering         │
│ Estimates at ≈4 characters per token.                │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

"Turn on metering" asks once, in a modal, before it writes `"meter": true` to `.smdrc` (R5).

```text
Turn on token metering for this workspace?

smd will record which .smd files and sections agents read and how many tokens they
received, in .smd/meter/ in this folder. Nothing leaves your machine. No document
text is stored. The folder is ignored by Git. You can turn it off or clear it at any time.

                                 [ Turn on ]  [ Cancel ]
```

### Metering on

```text
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 🤖 Agent token meter                  last 7 days    │
│                                                      │
│ Measured  · 61% saved (session net)                  │
│ 9 sessions · 14 reads · 31.4k tok served             │
│ ████████████████████░░░░░░░░░░░░  51.2k → 19.8k      │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ Estimate for this file                               │
│ Without smd · raw file          ≈6,312 tok           │
│ ████████████████████████                             │
│ With smd · agent view           ≈2,104 tok · 67% fewer│
│ ████████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░                             │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ Agents          Claude Code 9 · Codex 4 · Cursor 1   │
│ Bypassed smd    Claude Code 2 raw reads · others n/m │
│ Most read       Requirements 8 · Risks 5 · API 3     │
│ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ 📊 Open meter · 👁 Agent view · ☰ Left out · ⧉ Copy   │
│ ≈4 chars/token · session net savings · How counted?  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

- "n/m" means not measured. It is shown for agents without a raw-read hook, never 0 (R4).
- The period in the card is fixed at the last 7 days. The panel has the period picker.
- Negative session net savings show in the warning colour with the text "used more tokens than reading the file once", not hidden (AC5).

## Meter panel

Opened from the card, the status bar item or **Semantic Markdown: Open Token Meter**. It has four tabs and one period picker shared by all of them (R13).

::::tabs
:::tab Overview
```text
Token meter · workspace               Period: [ Last 30 days ▾ ]   Method: ≈4 chars/token

┌ Session net savings ─┐ ┌ Tokens served ──┐ ┌ smd share ──────┐ ┌ Targeted reads ┐
│ 412k  (63%)          │ │ 241k            │ │ 88%  Claude Code│ │ 72%            │
│ vs 653k baseline     │ │ 1,284 reads     │ │ n/m  others     │ │ section+query  │
└──────────────────────┘ └─────────────────┘ └─────────────────┘ └────────────────┘

Per-read savings (overstates, see How counted): 1.9M (89%)

Files                          Reads  Sessions  Baseline  Served  Saved
docs/requirements/prd.smd        412       61    184k     52k     72%  ████████▌
docs/rfcs/view-laws.smd          233       40    121k     49k     60%  ███████
architecture.smd                 190       35    150k     88k     41%  ████▊
editor.smd                        12        4     9.1k    11.2k   −23%  ▏ used more
…
```
:::

:::tab Sections
```text
Sections · docs/requirements/prd.smd ▾        Sort: [ Reads ▾ ]

Section               Reads  Sessions  Served   Re-reads  Last read
Requirements            98      52     21.0k      12%     today 10:22   ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓
  Recording             41      30      6.2k       5%     today 10:22   ▓▓▓▓
Risks                   55      38      8.8k       3%     yesterday     ▓▓▓▓▓▓
API                     31      17      9.4k      19%     Nov 17        ▓▓▓
Background               0       0         0        —     never         (agent=skip)
Rollout                  0       0         0        —     never         never read
Unmatched: "Old scope" 6 reads (heading renamed or removed)
```

Choosing a row opens the file at that heading.
:::

:::tab Graph
```text
Section graph · docs/requirements/prd.smd ▾    [x] co-read  [x] followed  [x] declared

        (Requirements 98) ━━━━━━━━ 34 ━━━━━━━━ (Risks 55)
              ┃  ╲                                 ┊
             21   ╲ 9 followed R1→C2              ┊ declared, never followed
              ┃     ╲                              ┊
          (API 31)  (Constraints 22)          (Rollout 0)

Findings
• Declared, never followed: Risks → Rollout (depends-on)
• Read together, not linked: Requirements ↔ API (21 sessions) — add a :ref?

[ Copy as Mermaid ]
```

Node size is reads, solid edges are co-reads (thicker means more sessions), arrows are followed dependencies and dashed edges are declared links (R11).
:::

