### Empty states

| State                          | Panel shows                                                                                                                                  |
| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Metering off                   | A short explanation, the same consent text as the modal and a **Turn on metering** button                                                    |
| On, no events                  | "No agent reads yet. Agents that read `.smd` files through the smd MCP server or CLI show up here." with links to `smd init --agent …` setup |
| Log over its size cap          | A warning bar, "Metering paused, the log reached 20 MB", with **Clear old events**                                                           |
| Mixed tokenizers in the period | A note under the KPIs naming both methods, with savings shown per method                                                                     |

## Heading hints

Off by default, turned on with `smd.meter.headingHints` (R14).

```text
   👁 98 reads · 52 sessions · last 7 days
12 ## Requirements
   👁 41 reads · 30 sessions
20 ### Recording
   👁 never read by agents
88 ## Rollout
```

## CLI report

`smd meter report` prints the same KPIs as the panel (R15).

```text
$ smd meter report --since 2026-11-01

Token meter · 2026-11-01 to 2026-11-19 · ≈4 chars/token

Session net savings   412,310 tokens (63%) vs 653,004 baseline
Tokens served         241,120 in 1,284 reads, 159 sessions
Per-read savings      1,902,775 (89%), overstates
smd share             89% Claude Code · not measured: Codex, Cursor
Targeted reads        72%   Re-reads 9%

Most read sections
  98  docs/requirements/prd.smd#requirements
  55  docs/requirements/prd.smd#risks
  41  docs/requirements/prd.smd#recording

Agents
  claude-code   41 sessions   802 reads   151,004 served
  codex         12 sessions   301 reads    58,210 served
  cursor         6 sessions   170 reads    29,020 served
```

`--json` prints the object `meterReport` returns, so CI or a notebook can read it.

## Open questions

::::question{#Q3 status=answered owner=@roshanmadhushanka due=2026-11-26} Should the status bar item open the panel or the agent view once metering is on?
The mock opens the panel, because the card already links to the agent view. People used to clicking for the agent view would lose that.

:::comment{for=Q3 date=2026-11-20 kind=answer}
Built as the mock shows when the maintainer asked to complete the work: with metering on the item opens the panel, and the card keeps its Agent view link. With metering off it opens the agent view as before. Reopen to change.
:::
::::

::::question{#Q4 status=answered owner=@roshanmadhushanka due=2026-11-26} Is the graph worth phase 5, or should the findings list ship alone first?
The two findings carry most of the value and need no layout code.

:::comment{for=Q4 date=2026-11-20 kind=answer}
Both were built: the findings list and a small inline SVG graph (nodes on a circle, no layout library), plus Copy as Mermaid. Reopen to drop the drawing.
:::
::::
